      "source": "T:Positive, continuous and decreasing on $[2, \\infty)$: decreasing fails ($x\\ln x$ is increasing, so $f$ is increasing)"
    },
    {
      "id": "st-f-009",
      "len": 118,
      "source": "T:$f(x) = \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{x^2}$ is not decreasing; limit comparison with $\\frac{1}{n^2}$ gives $L = 1$, so it diverges"
    },
    {
      "id": "ip-f-009",
      "len": 117,
      "source": "T:If the original integral reappears after integrating by parts, the choice of $u$ was wrong and you must start over."
